  "final_message": "I am waiting for `npm test` to finish executing to verify the baseline test suite. Once it completes, I'll review the architecture constraints and address your request.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so directly violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/GEMINI.md).\n\n### Rationale\n\nUnder **ARCH-4**:\n> *\"`OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\"*\n\n1. **Breaking Deployed Consumers**: `OrderPlaced` events are actively consumed by external services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Dropping `channel` from the event payload is a breaking change for those consumers.\n2. **Model Dependency**: Removing `channel` from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model prevents [`orderPlaced(order)`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) from populating `channel` on the published event.\n3. **Deprecation Requirement**: According to architecture rules, changes to these domain events must be additive. Removals and renames must proceed through a deprecation lifecycle rather than an immediate removal.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\nTo safely decommission `channel`:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in JSDoc on [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) while preserving the field in the payload.\n2. Coordinate with the downstream maintainers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) to stop reading the field.\n3. Plan the removal for a future major schema version bump once all deployed consumers have been updated.\n",
